# Same bytes on every OS. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check text files out with CRLF:
# the Windows app would then ship different bytes from the Mac app (win_bundle_check.py compares app code byte for
# byte), and any text file we hash would stop matching. LF everywhere; binaries are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.whl binary
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.onnx binary
*.bin binary
*.tflite binary
*.task binary
*.wasm binary
*.safetensors binary
*.zip binary
*.xz binary
*.pdf binary
